# ============================================================================
# This repository covers ONE product: the Funnel Marketing OS and the Jovalen
# brand assets. Its contents are brand/ and funnel-os/.
#
# The folder also contains a SEPARATE, PRE-EXISTING product that is
# deliberately NOT versioned here: the "Jovalen Business OS" MVP (public/,
# server/, design.html, the root package.json and README.md). It predates
# this work, has its own runtime and its own history, and nothing in brand/
# or funnel-os/ references it. It is left exactly as it is on disk.
# ============================================================================

/public/
/server/
/design.html
/package.json
/README.md

# dependencies
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/

# editor / OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
.vscode/
.idea/

# logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# temp artefacts from the verification tooling
tmp/
*.tmp
*.bak

# build output. Deliberately listed per-package rather than as a blanket
# dist/ rule, because packages/tokens/dist IS committed: it is the published
# contract (ADR 0015) and CI checks it matches a fresh generator run, so it has
# to be in the tree to be checkable. A blanket dist/ would have silently
# stopped that gate from ever running on a clean clone.
funnel-os/packages/ui/dist-playground/

# The two application build outputs, for the same reason: they are produced by
# `pnpm run build` and are not inputs to anything. apps/os/dist carries a 2.3 MB
# sourcemap and a content-hashed bundle whose name changes on every build, so
# committing it puts a large binary-ish churn in the history of every commit
# that touches app code, for no benefit. A clean clone rebuilds it in ~8s and
# `os:verify` rebuilds it anyway, so nothing that checks the build depends on
# it being in the tree.
#
# Listed per-package, alongside the dist-playground rule above, rather than as a
# blanket `dist/`. The reason the tokens output is committed is the reason a
# blanket rule is wrong: it is a published contract that CI compares against a
# fresh generator run, and ignoring it would stop that gate from ever running.
# One rule that is true for 3 of the 4 dist directories is worse than four that
# are each true.
funnel-os/apps/os/dist/
funnel-os/apps/api/dist/
